#!/bin/sh
# Runs a TypeScript entry with Node 24 or later, the one CI tests: the one on PATH when it is
# recent enough, else the newest one nvm installed. A hook runs with its session's PATH, which may
# hold an older Node set by a project.
recent() {
  v=$("$1" --version 2>/dev/null) || return 1
  v=${v#v}; major=${v%%.*}
  [ "$major" -ge 24 ]
}
for node in "$(command -v node)" $(ls -d "${NVM_DIR:-$HOME/.nvm}"/versions/node/v*/bin/node 2>/dev/null | sort -rV); do
  if [ -n "$node" ] && recent "$node"; then exec "$node" --import "$(dirname "$(readlink -f "$0")")/compile-cache.mjs" "$@"; fi
done
echo "agent-desk needs Node.js 24 or later, and the one on PATH is $(node --version 2>/dev/null || echo missing); install a newer one (nvm install 24) or put it on PATH" >&2
exit 1
